Vendored: Online Python Tutor — Python tracer
---------------------------------------------
  codeviz/vendor/pg_logger.py
  codeviz/vendor/pg_encoder.py

From Online Python Tutor (https://github.com/pgbovine/OnlinePythonTutor/),
Copyright (C) Philip J. Guo (philip@pgbovine.net), MIT License.

Local modifications:
  - removed `import imp` and replaced imp.new_module() with types.ModuleType()
    for Python 3.12+ compatibility
  - made two regex literals raw strings to silence SyntaxWarnings

The OPT trace JSON format (consumed by viewer_template.html and produced by the
JavaScript tracer) also originates from Online Python Tutor.

Original container tracers (C/C++, Java, x86-64 asm)
----------------------------------------------------
The C/C++ (GDB Python-API), Java (com.sun.jdi), and x86-64 assembly (qemu-user +
gdb-multiarch) tracers under codeviz/docker/ are codeviz's OWN work, MIT-licensed.
They do NOT vendor OPT's Valgrind backend or the AGPL java_jail / traceprinter —
those are not used. Built into images published to GHCR (pull-first) or built
locally from the in-repo contexts.

The JavaScript/TypeScript tracer (codeviz/tracers/js/trace.js) is likewise original
work for the modern V8 Inspector Protocol, NOT derived from OPT's jslogger.js.
